<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en" data-theme="light"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-6smd9voUY0VkyA6NT2acrI+jbKMEnJea/u0SMBWEj40='; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>S106 - Public probes versus the private dependency path</title>
  <script>
  (() => {
    const param = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("clawpilotTheme");
    const theme =
      param || (window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light");
    document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
  })();
  </script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer=""></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer=""></script>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <p class="training">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">S106 · A-S106 · SC-S106 · One frozen S unit</p>
      <h1>A public HTTP 200 is not a private-path certificate</h1>
      <p>Compare public and private probes; public success cannot certify a private dependency path.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="boundaries-heading">
      <h2 id="boundaries-heading">Fixed teaching observations only</h2>
      <p>Every client, DNS answer, connection, authorization, dependency and duration below is fictional <strong>DATA ONLY</strong>.
        These controls do not run probes, change networks or identity, resolve DNS, access resources or contact any service.</p>
      <p>The required client is <code>application-private-segment</code>, DNS must report <code>private-address-label</code>,
        and the journey must reach <code>orders-private-label</code> within <strong>150 synthetic ms</strong>.
        Management access must remain unexposed.</p>
      <p>Public endpoint and internal process health are distinct scopes. Missing or unrelated private observations remain unknown,
        even when either health check is successful. A complete synthetic comparison is not native private connectivity proof.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="operator-heading">
      <h2 id="operator-heading">1. Choose and record</h2>
      <form id="probe-form">
        <label for="condition">Teaching condition</label>
        <select id="condition" name="condition">
          <option value="private-ready" selected="">Complete private-path teaching trace</option>
          <option value="dns-public-answer">Private client gets a public DNS answer</option>
          <option value="connection-denied">Private connection denied</option>
          <option value="authorization-denied">Dependency authorization denied</option>
          <option value="wrong-client">Successful probe from an unrelated client</option>
          <option value="wrong-dependency">HTTP 200 from the wrong dependency</option>
          <option value="private-unobserved">No private-path observations</option>
          <option value="dns-unobserved">Private DNS answer not observed</option>
          <option value="management-exposed">Private path works but management is exposed</option>
          <option value="dependency-slow">Private HTTP 200 exceeds the journey budget</option>
        </select>
        <label for="operator-action">Operator action</label>
        <select id="operator-action" name="operatorAction">
          <option value="public-only" selected="">Record public probe only</option>
          <option value="public-internal">Record public and internal health only</option>
          <option value="compare-private">Compare with the private teaching trace</option>
        </select>
        <div class="buttons">
          <button id="record-probes" type="submit">Record teaching comparison</button>
          <button id="reset-lesson" type="button" class="secondary">Reset current exercise</button>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">Keyboard: Tab between controls, arrow keys to choose, Enter to record or reset.
          Reset restores defaults and focus, but retains history and the 12-record allowance. Reload starts a new in-memory session.</p>
        <p id="input-error" class="error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden=""></p>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section id="assessment" class="panel" data-status="unknown" aria-labelledby="results-heading" aria-live="polite">
      <h2 id="results-heading">2. Keep the probe scopes separate</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Public endpoint probe</dt><dd id="public-result">success - HTTP 200; 24 synthetic ms; public endpoint only</dd>
        <dt>Internal process health</dt><dd id="internal-result">success - HTTP 200; 18 synthetic ms; process health only</dd>
        <dt>Observed private-probe client label</dt><dd id="observed-client">application-private-segment</dd>
        <dt>Required private-path duration</dt><dd id="private-duration">84 synthetic ms; budget 150 synthetic ms</dd>
      </dl>
      <h3 id="private-outcome">Actual private path in the teaching trace: unknown</h3>
      <p id="eligibility">Not eligible - actual private-path or management-safety gate not satisfied</p>
      <p id="explanation">Public/internal success is not private-path proof. Missing required private observations remain unknown.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <caption>Private applicability, dependency and management-safety observations</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Required check</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Fixed observation and expectation</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="private-checks"><tr data-check="placement" data-status="success"><td>Application client placement</td><td>success</td><td>Observed probe client: application-private-segment; expected application-private-segment</td></tr><tr data-check="dns" data-status="unknown"><td>Private DNS answer</td><td>unknown</td><td>Unknown - not observed</td></tr><tr data-check="connectivity" data-status="success"><td>Private connectivity</td><td>success</td><td>Observed connectivity: true; expected true</td></tr><tr data-check="authorization" data-status="success"><td>Dependency authorization</td><td>success</td><td>Observed dependency authorization: true; expected true</td></tr><tr data-check="dependency" data-status="success"><td>Required dependency journey</td><td>success</td><td>Observed orders-private-label; HTTP 200; 84 synthetic ms. Required orders-private-label; HTTP 200; budget 150 synthetic ms</td></tr><tr data-check="management" data-status="success"><td>Management access remains unexposed</td><td>success</td><td>Observed management exposure: false; expected false</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="history-heading">
      <h2 id="history-heading">3. Retained page-session history</h2>
      <p id="counts" aria-live="polite">Attempts 10/12 | Private success 1 | Private failure 4 | Private unknown 5</p>
      <p id="separate-probes">Public successes 10; internal successes 9. Neither is the private-path success numerator.</p>
      <p>Private successes + failures + unknowns include every recorded comparison. Later success or reset does not erase an earlier failure.
        An empty session is no evidence, not 100% success.</p>
      <ol id="history" aria-label="All recorded teaching comparisons"><li data-status="unknown">#1 private-ready / public-only: private unknown; public success; internal unknown; not eligible.</li><li data-status="unknown">#2 private-ready / public-internal: private unknown; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li><li data-status="failure">#3 dns-public-answer / compare-private: private failure; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li><li data-status="success">#4 private-ready / compare-private: private success; public success; internal success; synthetic fixture eligible.</li><li data-status="failure">#5 connection-denied / compare-private: private failure; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li><li data-status="failure">#6 authorization-denied / compare-private: private failure; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li><li data-status="unknown">#7 wrong-client / compare-private: private unknown; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li><li data-status="failure">#8 wrong-dependency / compare-private: private failure; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li><li data-status="unknown">#9 private-unobserved / compare-private: private unknown; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li><li data-status="unknown">#10 dns-unobserved / compare-private: private unknown; public success; internal success; not eligible.</li></ol>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="exercise-heading">
      <h2 id="exercise-heading">Try the misleading success</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose the public-DNS-answer condition. Record public only: the private path is <strong>unknown</strong>.</li>
        <li>Compare the private trace: public/internal health still succeeds, but private DNS <strong>fails</strong>.</li>
        <li>Compare the complete trace: placement, DNS, connectivity, authorization, dependency and unexposed management all pass
          in this fixed synthetic fixture.</li>
        <li>Try the unrelated client: its HTTP 200 does not diagnose the actual private path. Reset and inspect the retained history.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="hint">IaC N/A. No cloud, deployment, credentials, live identity, frameworks or packages.
        B-S106 and D-S106 remain unqualified; this lesson does not validate production Node 24, native Azure or five-nines reliability.</p>
    </section>
    <noscript><p class="error">Enable local JavaScript to use the teaching exercise. No network or Azure account is required.</p></noscript>
  </main>


</body></html>